{
 "title": "U-Net (segmentation)",
 "description": "U-Net as in milesial/Pytorch-UNet (bilinear=False): an encoder of DoubleConv and four Down steps (64 → 1024 channels, 256 → 16 pixels), a decoder of four Up steps that double the size with a transposed convolution and join the encoder's map at the same size (the skip connections), and a 1×1 convolution to a score per class per pixel. Trained with per-pixel cross-entropy against a mask of class indices. 31,037,698 parameters, the same as the reference.",
